cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "pse-opendata-mcp: MCP server for Polish power-system data from the public reports of PSE"
abstract: >-
  A Model Context Protocol server that lets LLM assistants query Polish power-system data (day-ahead prices,
  demand, wind and PV generation, net cross-border flows, curtailment of renewables, the balancing market) from
  the public reports of PSE S.A., the Polish transmission system operator, through the pse-opendata library.
  Answers are aggregated by default, capped, and state source, retrieval time, time zone and units once.
  Not affiliated with PSE S.A.
authors:
  - family-names: "Waleszczyński"
    given-names: "Konrad"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-16"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/kwwaleszczynski-del/pse-opendata-mcp"
keywords:
  - model context protocol
  - electricity market
  - power system
  - Poland
  - open data
